Designs: Show the table names in the menu of Editor (hever)

The design hides the text of the link to select data and keeps only its
icon. In Adminer that link is a separate one, next to the link with the
table name, so hiding its text is right. In Editor there is a single link
per table and it carries the name, so the menu showed a column of icons
without any name.

The rule is restricted to body.adminer, that Adminer sets and Editor does
not, as it already is in konya, rmsoft, rmsoft_blue and rmsoft_blue-dark.
The scoping was lost when hever was updated to 0.3.3.

--- a/designs/hever/adminer.css	2026-10-05 11:39:41.030183379 +0000
+++ b/designs/hever/adminer.css	2026-10-05 11:39:41.046998885 +0000
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
   #menu .links a:hover {color:light-dark(red, #f88);}
 }
 
-#menu ul#tables a[href*="&select="] {background:url("data:image/png;base64,") no-repeat scroll right bottom; display:inline-block; height:16px; margin-right:4px; vertical-align:middle; overflow:hidden; padding-left:16px; width:0;}
+body.adminer #menu ul#tables a[href*="&select="] {background:url("data:image/png;base64,") no-repeat scroll right bottom; display:inline-block; height:16px; margin-right:4px; vertical-align:middle; overflow:hidden; padding-left:16px; width:0;}
 #menu ul#tables a.active[href*="&select="] {border-left:2px solid light-dark(blue, #99d); margin-left:-4px; padding-left:18px;}
 
 .links a[href*="&create="] {background:url("data:image/png;base64,") no-repeat scroll 2px bottom; padding-left:22px;}
